From 5aed3a491c4c42b8ccfbc9e0b1961e3fda752d2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:43:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/19] Verify eth_getBlockByHash answers with failover so one
 faulty RPC cannot wedge historical calls
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Helios's historical path calls eth_getBlockByHash(hash, true) before its EIP-2935 history proof. The gateway passed
the first answer through, so a liar's block was all Helios ever got. That is the failed control, now a test.

* network/witness-gateway.mjs, when proofs are configured: eth_getBlockByHash [hash, fullTx] tries the upstreams in
  order, and each answer is checked by the witness-check `block` op.
  - The header must hash to the requested hash; the upstream's hash field is never trusted. The Base header rules
    apply.
  - With fullTx, the body must pass Helios's OpStack::validate_block.
  - An invalid answer costs its source the try. null is served only if every answering source said null and none
    answered with an invalid block. The verifier unavailable means a refusal.
  - A hash-only answer is HEADER-verified only (stats.blocksHeaderOnly).
  - Blocks are served as received, and never cached or used as roots.
  - New stats: per-upstream blockOk/blockInvalid/blockNull; blocksFull/blocksHeaderOnly.
  - Without proofs, the old plain behavior is unchanged.
* test/witness-blocks.test.mjs (real helper; real full blocks derived from the 52 signed gossip objects):
  - all 52 verify full;
  - 10 forged or wrong-body first answers are refused and the real block is served; with the liar alone, refused;
  - nothing is cached or bound;
  - a FAILED CONTROL (plain path) serves the forgery;
  - null, oversize, hung, deadline and dead-verifier cases;
  - the header-only BOUNDARY, asserted explicitly.
* test/helios-block-failover.e2e.test.mjs: real Helios on real heads 80→106. The forged first block is refused and
  the real full block served, and Helios goes on to its history proof. The control run shows the liar's block served.
* test/helios-real-history.e2e.test.mjs (from 7b4dd692): its honest source now answers the full-body request with the
  real full block (exportBlock). Before, it sent a bare header, which this gateway now correctly refuses.
